cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this proof or checker, cite this archive and the sources listed in README.md."
title: "Stewart’s existence conjecture for three perfect powers in square-root intervals"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Yongxian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-3864-3536"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
abstract: "A square, a cube, and a fifth power occur in infinitely many intervals from N through N plus the square root of N, with an explicit count and an exactly-three refinement for the constructed family. This proves the existence part of Stewart’s 2008 conjecture, not the separate universal upper bound."
